//! Named-view help (V12).

pub(super) const HELP: &str = "Model views (V12): named views with their own view plane and display properties, kept in a session JSON file beside the model; the store is never written. list-views --file FILE returns the folders and every view. save-view --file FILE --name NAME creates a view from exactly one plane: an orbit --yaw RAD --pitch RAD [--target X,Y,Z]; a coordinate plane --parallel xy|xz|yz [--offset MM]; an explicit frame --plane OX,OY,OZ,XX,XY,XZ,YX,YY,YZ; --two-points A;B (vertical, or across the input plane given by --work-plane); --three-points A;B;C; or, reading the model through --store ROOT: --grid SELECTOR --axis LABEL (one axis) or --grid SELECTOR [--u-axes none|first|last|all] [--v-axes ...] [--u-prefix TEXT] [--v-prefix TEXT] (one view per axis, named prefix and label), --level NAME|ID or --levels first|last|all, --element ID or --assembly ID with --side front|back|top|bottom|end|3d|four (four creates front, top, end and 3d), and --ray-origin X,Y,Z --ray-direction X,Y,Z [--edge A;B] (the first face hit). Batches add all views or none and suffix repeated names. Display properties, for save-view and update-view: --projection, --span MM (visible height), --depth none|ABOVE,BELOW (distance shown towards the viewer and behind the plane), --rotation Z_DEG,X_DEG (turns the camera, not the plane), --render-mode, --grids, --hidden-kinds none|KIND,..., --work-area none|six numbers, --color default|R,G,B (0..1), --opacity 0..1, --folder PATH, --favorite, --copy-from VIEW. update-view --file FILE --view ID|NAME [--name NEW] changes one view, its plane through any single-view option. remove-view and apply-view take --view ID|NAME; apply-view returns the view, its camera frame and its clip planes, without touching any store.";
